course: dictionary
lesson: 8670
title: Secretly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Secretly» is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and it means in a way that other people do not see or know about. «She was surprised and secretly pleased.» Others could see her surprise, but her happiness stayed hidden inside her.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. «Kenzie says, "Try livin' wi' him," but secretly she loves it.» The word «but» shows that her words and her real feeling do not match, so she is keeping her love hidden.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a phrase such as «in secret» or «without anyone knowing». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Secrets can be safe or unsafe. A surprise party for Mum is a good secret that you will share later. If an adult asks you to keep a secret from your parents, especially about touching or presents, tell a trusted adult straight away.
fact: «Secretly» is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Secretly» means in a way that other people do not see or know about.
fact: «Secretly» can describe a feeling you keep inside and do not show, like «secretly glad».
fact: «Secretly planned» means someone made plans that others did not know about, such as a surprise party.
fact: Good surprises are fine to keep quiet about for a while, but bad secrets are not. Always tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «She was surprised and secretly pleased.» What does secretly mean here? | Very quickly and angrily | Loudly and with a big smile | Out loud, so everyone heard | *In a way that others cannot see, so her happiness stayed hidden
exercise: «Kenzie says, "Try livin' wi' him," but secretly she loves it.» Which word shows that her words and her real feeling do not match? | try | says | loves | *but
exercise: An adult asks you to keep a secret from your parents about touching. What should you do? | Wait and see if it goes away | *Tell a trusted adult straight away | Promise, then tell nobody ever | Keep it secret, because adults are always right
test: «The team secretly planned a surprise party for Mum.» What does secretly tell you? | That the party was cancelled | That the team forgot the party | *That the team made plans that Mum did not know about | That the team was very loud about the party
test: Which kind of secret must you tell a trusted adult? | A present you are making for your sister | A birthday cake hidden in the fridge | *A secret an adult asks you to keep from your parents | A surprise party for your gran
exam: He ___ hoped the team would win, and nobody guessed how much he cared. | angrily | slowly | *secretly | loudly
